F1 (medium, false green — needs an L1 rule decision before it lands): an efi chainload entry whose
image line is not a pin (no `#hash`, the common real-world shape) is reported HEALTHY rc 0 even
when the file is absent, because R2 makes a hashless value not a pin and R6 keys the panic on a pin
on the image line. Limine v12.9.4 chainload.c 426-435 calls uri_open on that path regardless and
panics "Failed to open image". Adding a pin would break the frozen 73-family pins lists; an additive
top-level key is allowed by the GATE OUTPUT CONTRACT ("Other extra keys are allowed and ignored") and
changes no existing field. The docstring's Output line should gain the key if this lands.

